AI ChatBot Project
A lightweight, role-playing AI chatbot implementation developed in Python using the OpenAI API and configured within a containerized Linux DevOps environment.

📌 Project Overview
The AI ChatBot project is designed to instantiate a custom-configured conversational assistant acting as a friendly travel guide. It connects securely to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint using environment-based authentication and interacts with custom chat models under strict parameter constraints (temperature and token limits).

🚀 Key Features & Implementation Details
Dynamic Client Configuration: Initializes the OpenAI client dynamically, reading OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_API_BASE directly from system environment variables (populated via /root/.bash_profile).

Role-Play Persona: Utilizes a structured system/user prompt workflow instructing the model to behave as an engaging and helpful travel guide.

Controlled Generation Parameters: Configured with temperature=0.7 for balanced creativity and max_tokens=100 for concise responses.

Isolated Execution Environment: Built and run inside a dedicated Python virtual environment (venv) with all required dependency management handled securely.

